course: dictionary
lesson: 12945
title: Excel: being outstanding
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To excel means to be extremely good at something, better than most other people. «Maya excels at maths» tells you she is not just good at it, she is one of the best. The clue is better than most others.
explain: You can excel in sport, art, music or spelling. «Sam excels in football» means Sam is very skilled at football. Excel at and excel in both mean being outstanding at something.
explain: To excel yourself means to do even better than you usually do. «Ben wanted to excel himself, so he practised every day and beat his own best time.» Ask: is this better than Ben's usual best? Yes, so it fits.
explain: With a capital E, Excel is the name of a computer program used for spreadsheets, which keep tables, sums and charts. Here it is a name, not a verb: «We put the costs into Excel.» Look for the capital letter to tell the two uses apart.
fact: Excel means to be extremely good at something, better than most others.
fact: Excel is often followed by at or in: excel at, excel in.
fact: «Excelled» is the past form: «She excelled at reading last year.»
fact: To excel yourself means to do better than you usually do.
fact: Excel with a capital E is a computer program that makes tables, sums and charts.
exercise: «Priya excels at drawing.» What does excels mean here? | Is afraid of | Is sometimes late for | *Is extremely good at | Is bored by
exercise: «Sam tried hard to excel himself in the test.» What does excel himself mean? | *Do better than he usually does | Copy his friend's answers | Forget everything he knows | Give up early
exercise: Mum says, «We will make the sums and chart in Excel.» What is Excel here? | A place to swim | *A computer program for tables and charts | A kind of cake | A type of sport
test: What does excelled mean in «Tom excelled in spelling last term»? | Was very late for | Was afraid of | *Was extremely good at | Forgot about
test: Which sentence uses Excel as a computer program? | «He excelled himself today.» | «They excel in music.» | «She excels at chess.» | *«We put the costs into Excel.»
exam: Which word completes «Ava will ___ at swimming if she keeps training»? | cover | *excel | forget | dislike
